  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r1779/02\r1779/01 REV A\r1779/00\rNoise Impact Assessment Report\rAnalysis of site layout for daylight and sunlight\r\rReason: To ensure the development proceeds in accordance with the approved plans.\r",
    "Prior to the commencement of the relevant works, detailed drawings, material details, and specifications of the proposed boundary treatment, cycle storage, and refuse storage shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall thereafter be carried out in accordance with the approved details.\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "Prior to occupation of the development, the refuse storage facilities shown on drawing number 1779/01 shall be provided in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "Prior to first occupation of the development cycle parking, shall be provided as indicated on drawing 1779/01, in accordance with the following requirements:\r\r- Provision of a minimum of 1 long stay cycle parking spaces;\r\r- in an accessible location; the store door must have a minimum opening width of 1.2m\r\r- long stay cycle parking spaces secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\r- fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities and to safeguard the character and appearance of the area.\r"
